Expose PutNewWindow + CoreWebView2 for host-managed popups

Adds the plumbing needed to support "deferred popup" pages — those that do:

  const popup = window.open('placeholder', '_blank');
  fetch(...).then(d => popup.location = d.realUrl);

Previously the host had to either let WebView2 open its default empty popup
or call PutHandled(true) and create its own window — but in the latter case
the site has no live Window reference, so popup.location = ... fails with
TypeError and the redirect never lands.

New surface:
- ICoreWebView2NewWindowRequestedEventArgs.PutNewWindow(*ICoreWebView2)
- Chromium.CoreWebView2() accessor for the raw ICoreWebView2
- WebView.OnNewWindowRequestedRaw — variant of OnNewWindowRequested that
  does NOT auto-PutHandled, so the handler can choose between Handled
  (suppress) or NewWindow (host-managed).
- WebView.CoreWebView2() — convenience to fetch the raw pointer from a
  high-level webview.
